-gray-100\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"h2\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-2xl font-bold mb-6\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"❓ Frequently Asked Questions\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"space-y-3\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"details\\\",\\\"0\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"summary\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Why choose a geographical name?\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Geographical names are distinctive, personal, and tell a story. They're great conversation starters.\\\"}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"details\\\",\\\"1\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"summary\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Which geographic name is trending in 2026?\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Mountain and summit names are the fastest-growing geographic naming trend: Everest, Denali, Zion, Sierra, and Atlas have all risen sharply. City names are also trending — Brooklyn, Sydney, Aspen, Austin, and Savannah lead the pack. River names (Nile, Amazon, Hudson, Jordan) remain perennially popular and show no signs of fading.\\\"}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"details\\\",\\\"2\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"summary\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Can I use a place name from a country I've never visited?\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Yes — many pet owners choose place names based on the sound and feeling of the name rather than personal travel history. 'Kyoto' sounds elegant regardless of whether you've been to Japan. What matters is that the name resonates with you. That said, learning a bit about the place you name your pet after adds a wonderful layer of meaning to the name.\\\"}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"details\\\",\\\"3\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"summary\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Are geographic names too long or complicated for pets?\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Most popular geographic names are surprisingly short and simple: Aspen, Rio, Zion, Nile, Oslo, Paris, Sydney — all two syllables or fewer. You can always use a shorter nickname for longer place names. 'Mississippi' can become 'Missi,' and 'Saskatchewan' can become 'Sassy.' The full name carries the meaning; the nickname carries the daily call.\\\"}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"details\\\",\\\"4\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"summary\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"What geographic names work best for different pet personalities?\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Adventurous, outdoorsy pets suit mountain and wilderness names (Denali, Zion, Aspen, Sierra, River). Elegant, graceful pets match well with city names (Paris, Vienna, Florence, Kyoto). Calm, gentle pets pair beautifully with nature names (Meadow, Forest, Ocean, Coral). Quirky, funny pets can carry unexpected place names with charm (Topeka, Kalamazoo, Walla Walla).\\\"}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"details\\\",\\\"5\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"summary\\\",null,{